# Local build and boot

- Compile with RosBE 2.2.1 and Clang 18.1.8. `ARCH=amd64` is the only supported OS build. 32-bit applications run on that boot. The daily boot config is Clang 18.1.8, amd64, Debug, target `bootcd`. Boot tests use QEMU 11.1.0.
- `tools/pipeline/Build-Bootcd.ps1` writes `build-amd64/bootcd.iso`.
- `tools/pipeline/Test-Boot.ps1` runs `C:\Program Files\qemu\qemu-system-x86_64.exe -accel tcg -m 8192 -smp 4`. Do not pass `-accel whpx`. Windows 10 22H2 boots use the same memory and CPU count.
- Load `tools/qemu-harness/abi.dll` with `-plugin`. It logs `SYSENTER`, `SYSCALL`, `INT 2E`, and calls into mapped `ntoskrnl`, `hal`, and `wdf` exports.
- Serial logs, plugin JSONL, and crash JSON go under `output/`. Do not commit `build/` or `output/`.
- Commands and the WHPX follow-up are in `docs/LOCAL_BUILD.md`.
